* Fender Bassman 5F6-A (tweed, 1959) preamp, from the schematic in R. Kuehnel's "The Fender Bassman 5F6-A Circuit" (Pentode Press):
* V1 12AY7 (two independent stages, bright and normal channel, each with a full #1 and a -6 dB #2 input), their volume pots
* mixed through 270k into V2a (12AX7, 820 cathode), V2b cathode follower, and the 5F6-A tone stack (250p, 56k, two 0.02 caps,
* 250k treble, 1M bass, 25k middle). The long-tailed phase inverter and the presence control are in poweramp.net.
*
* Assumptions where the drawing is silent or ambiguous (change them here, not in code):
*  - the jacks: the grid sits behind a 68k stopper from the #1 jack (1M to ground there); the #2 jack goes through another 68k and
*    the unplugged #1 jack grounds its contact: a 136k input, 6 dB down (SW_ resistors, set by the jack modes in amp.json);
*  - "Jumpered" feeds the same signal into both #1 jacks;
*  - V1's two cathodes share one 820 ohm with 250u; V2a's 820 is bypassed with 0.68u (the drawing prints a cap there, the text says
*    it is not a large one, the Marshall copy uses 0.68u);
*  - supply: the 385 V node (x) comes from the power amp; 10k and 8u make the 325 V rail of V1 and V2.

.nodes x nb gin in jb1 jb2 jn1 jn2 gb gn pb pn kk cb cn wb wn g2 p2a k2a k2b m t o u v wm

* The 385 V node (driven from the power amp at run time; 385 V is the standalone default).
V VRAIL x 100 385
R R10K x nb 10k
C C8U nb 0 8u
* The guitar behind a variable source resistance, then the jack switches.
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance. RSRC is the plain 7k source: the "Off" setting, and what a pedal in front of the amp
* looks like. A pickup replaces it with its own impedance as seen from the open-circuit voltage (the recording): the
* coil (winding resistance RPU + inductance) in parallel with its winding capacitance CPU and an eddy-current loss resistor
* RPL, then the cable capacitance (200 pF per 2 m, switched in steps of 200, 400 and 800 pF). The engine sets the values:
* single coil = coil 1 (2.5 H), humbucker and P-90 = coil 2 (5 H) with their own resistances; open = 1e12.
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

* Jacks, bright channel. SW_BJ1 / SW_BJ2: the plug is in #1 / #2; SW_BGND: the unplugged #1 contact grounds its node.
R SW_BJ1 in jb1 1
R RLEAK_B jb1 0 1M
R SW_BGND jb1 0 1e12
R R68_B1 jb1 gb 68k
R SW_BJ2 in jb2 1e12
R R68_B2 jb2 gb 68k
* Jacks, normal channel.
R SW_NJ1 in jn1 1e12
R RLEAK_N jn1 0 1M
R SW_NGND jn1 0 1
R R68_N1 jn1 gn 68k
R SW_NJ2 in jn2 1e12
R R68_N2 jn2 gn 68k

* V1: two 12AY7 triodes, 100k plate loads, one shared 820 / 250u cathode.
T V1B gb pb kk 12AY7
T V1A gn pn kk 12AY7
R R_PB nb pb 100k
R R_PN nb pn 100k
R RK1 kk 0 820
C CK1 kk 0 250u

* Bright channel: 0.02 coupling, 1M volume with the 100p bright cap across its top, 270k mixing resistor.
C C_B pb cb 20n
R VR_BT cb wb 1
R VR_BB wb 0 1
C C_BRIGHT cb wb 100p
R R270_B wb g2 270k
* Normal channel.
C C_N pn cn 20n
R VR_NT cn wn 1
R VR_NB wn 0 1
R R270_N wn g2 270k

* V2a (100k load, 820 cathode with 0.68u) and V2b, the cathode follower (100k cathode load).
T V2A g2 p2a k2a 12AX7
R R_P2A nb p2a 100k
R RK2A k2a 0 820
C CK2A k2a 0 0.68u
T V2B p2a nb k2b 12AX7
R R100K k2b 0 100k

* Tone stack: 250p and 56k from the follower, treble 250k pot (wiper = output), bass 1M rheostat, middle 25k pot, two 0.02 caps.
R R56K k2b m 56k
C C250T k2b t 250p
R VR_TT t o 1
R VR_TB o u 1
C C02A m u 20n
R VR_BASS u v 1
R VR_MT v wm 1
R VR_MB wm 0 1
C C02B m wm 20n

* Load of the phase-inverter input network.
R RPI o 0 1M
